# Memory (host-used delta, GB) vs mean concurrency
# Source: docs/reports/moca-side-by-side-report.md, completed measurement grid
# Metric: host-used delta (peak − baseline)
#
# All lines pass through the origin (zero sandboxes = zero memory).
#
# ── fc warm ──
# Duty-invariant, linear from origin.
#   Slope = 4.3/14 = 0.307 GB/sandbox.
#   Check: predicts 12.3 at N=40; measured 12.5 — linear model holds.
#
# ── fc perexec D=10% ──
# Two-component model, calibrated against the no-op run:
#   (a) base: VM machinery (jailer, memfile maps, wrapper cold reads).
#       No-op load80 peak: 2.8 GB at N=40.  Scales ~linearly with N.
#       Slope_base ≈ 0.07 GB/sandbox.
#   (b) cold-rootfs: host page-cache fill from in-flight cold reads.
#       At load50 (pre-knee): 2.6 − 0.98 = 1.62 GB for N=14.
#       At load80 (post-knee): 13.3 − 2.8 = 10.5 GB for N=40.
#       The 6.5× jump for 2.9× the concurrency is queueing amplification
#       past the CPU saturation knee (78% mean, queue → 76–87 effective).
#
# ── fc perexec D=2% (predicted) ──
# Same base term (VM machinery is per-sandbox, duty-independent).
# Cold-rootfs scales with in-flight count (N×D): at D=2%, 5× fewer.
#   Pre-knee cold-rootfs slope = 1.62/14 = 0.116 GB/sandbox at D=10%.
#   At D=2%: slope_cold = 0.116 × 0.2 = 0.023 GB/sandbox.
#   Total = 0.07 + 0.023 = 0.093 GB/sandbox (linear, pre-knee).
#   Knee at D=2%: CPU ≈ 4.65×0.02 = 0.093 cores/sandbox → N ≈ 200+.
#
# "?" = missing data (gnuplot skips the point)
#
# concurrency  fc_warm  fc_perexec_10pct  fc_perexec_2pct_predicted
0               0.0      0.0               0.0
14              4.3      2.6               1.3
40              12.5     13.3              3.7
80              ?        ?                 7.4
